<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bushire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bushire is an older European spelling of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushehr">Bushehr</a>, a port on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a>, the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">VOC</a> maintained commercial presences there. The Bushire trade gave the Zand state access to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> goods such as Indian textiles, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bushire.jpg" alt="Bushire" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hossein Heidarpour · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bushehr_City.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
